        "explanation": "<p>Using Charles's Law: $V_1/T_1 = V_2/T_2$. Convert temperatures to Kelvin: $T_1 = 27 + 273 = 300 K$, $T_2 = 77 + 273 = 350 K$. Solving for $V_2$: $V_2 = (V_1 \times T_2) / T_1 = (400 \times 350) / 300 = 466.67 cm^3$.</p>",
